.env
__pycache__/
*.pyc
trading_log.txt
backtest_trades*.csv
orders_export.csv
equity_history_export.csv

# watchlist_state.json and daily_risk_state.json are DELIBERATELY
# tracked (not ignored) -- the GitHub Actions workflow commits them
# back after every run so state survives between the fresh checkouts
# each scheduled run gets. See .github/workflows/trade.yml.
#
# logs/ and trades.csv are tracked for the SAME reason, but a different
# purpose: not state the next run needs, but evidence a human (or Claude)
# needs afterwards. A GitHub Actions runner is destroyed when its job
# ends, so anything not committed back is unrecoverable -- which is why
# diagnosing the 2026-07-24 failures meant reproducing them locally
# rather than reading what the bot had actually logged. logs/ keeps the
# terminal output per trading day; trades.csv keeps every trade with the
# indicator context behind it. Old logs are pruned after
# LOG_RETENTION_DAYS so the repo can't grow without bound.
#
# trading_log.txt above is the legacy single-file local log, superseded
# by logs/<date>.log -- still ignored so an old local copy doesn't get
# committed by accident.
